#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:1
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:3
msgid ""
"Words this project uses in a particular way. Each entry says where the "
"idea is treated properly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md
msgid "run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:7
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"One invocation of `freeports`. A run is one or more {term}`jobs <job>`, "
"and everything they produce is accumulated and written **once**, at the "
"end, as one set of tables. Running two reports in one run is therefore "
"not the same as running them twice — see {doc}`../overview/how-it-works`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:5
msgid "job"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:12
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"One report, read with one {term}`format`, against one set of target "
"companies. Jobs come from repeated `--input` or from the rows of a batch "
"CSV ({doc}`../guides/user/advanced/batch`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:9
msgid "format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:16
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The recipe for one report layout, named for the issuer, the language and "
"the earliest publication year it reads — `EURIZON-EN23`. The name follows"
" the recipe, not the document: a later report the same recipe still reads"
" keeps the name, and only a report that needs a recipe of its own gets a "
"new one. {doc}`../guides/formats/index`, {doc}`formats/names`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:15
msgid "formats repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:22
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A repository holding formats, their tests and their validation documents,"
" maintained independently of the engine. Created with `freeports-dev "
"init-format-repo`. {doc}`../guides/formats/repository`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:20
msgid "input database"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:27
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A directory of CSV files saying **which companies a run looks for** and "
"how to recognise each one. Separate from the engine and from any formats "
"repository, because which companies matter is a question about your work "
"rather than about parsing PDFs. {doc}`../guides/input-db/index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:25
msgid "bud"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:32
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A fragment of a company name used to recognise it in a report — the part "
"that survives the variations issuers introduce. {doc}`../guides/input-db"
"/recognising-companies`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:29
msgid "target list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:36
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A named set of companies within an input database. A run needs at least "
"one, and refuses immediately if none is given. {doc}`../guides/input-db"
"/target-lists`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:33
msgid "page class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:40
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"What kind of page this is, decided per document before any extraction "
"happens. Classification is itself a pipeline. "
"{doc}`design/classification`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:37
msgid "schedule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:44
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The ordered list of work for a run: the classified pages of every "
"document, poured together and processed in steps, where each step's "
"results filter the next. {doc}`design/schedule`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:41
msgid "pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:48
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"What a page of a given class goes through: three {term}`segments "
"<segment>` — `pdf_extract` → `text_filter` → `deserialize`. A class runs "
"a *bundle* of them. {doc}`design/segments`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:46
msgid "segment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:53
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"One of the three stages of a pipeline, answering one separable question: "
"what is on this page, does any of it concern us, what do the survivors "
"mean. {doc}`design/segments`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:50
msgid "promise"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:57
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A placeholder for a value a page genuinely could not know, resolved at "
"the end of the run against everything the run learned. "
"{doc}`design/promises`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:54
msgid "entity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:61
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"What the project models and ultimately writes out — the thing a resolved "
"extraction becomes. {doc}`design/entities-and-output`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:58
msgid "profile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:65
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A choice of what shape the output takes: which tables are written and "
"where. {doc}`../guides/user/output`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:62
msgid "grant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:69
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A signed statement that a named {term}`methodology` was applied to a "
"specific file, recorded against that file's hash — and therefore "
"invalidated by any change to the file, deliberately. "
"{doc}`../guides/grants/index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:67
msgid "methodology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:74
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A published document describing a protocol under which a grant may be "
"made. It is a document at an address the granter chose to trust, not a "
"value stored in the grant. {doc}`cli/methodology-sources`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:72
msgid "validation document"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:79
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"One YAML file per contributor, at `<repo>/validation/<name>.yaml`, signed"
" with their key, holding every grant that person has made in that "
"repository. {doc}`cli/freeports-validate`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:77
msgid "assertion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:84
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A statement about this software, written as prose, that a person can read"
" and agree with. Grants over assertions are made under *agreement and "
"good faith* rather than over bytes a program wrote. "
"{doc}`../validation/index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:82
msgid "metric"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:89
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A dotted name, a unit and a cost class, with a minimum in `ci.yaml`. "
"Distinct from a **suite**, which has an outcome rather than a number. "
"{doc}`../guides/devops/ci-yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:86
msgid "branch class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/glossary.md:93
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Which of `dev`, `pre` or `prod` a branch belongs to, derived from its "
"name at every run and never recorded. It decides what the gate refuses. "
"{doc}`../guides/devops/the-gate`."
msgstr ""

